			<div class="content" id="post-content-2308360">
									

<h1><span>Butterfly Effect</span></h1>
<h3><span>noun</span></h3>
<p>1. the idea, used in chaos theory, that a very small difference in the initial state of a physical system can make a significant difference to the state at some later time.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The anomalous thing about 2472 is its potential. Just imagine, all that anomalous mess at the end, trickling back down the chain of causation, all the way back to one little air coupler.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

