														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2308379">
									

<p>Not at all sure how I feel about this. If this is a redoing of that deleted tale about 2472 causing the end of the world, this is a much better take on it, but it just feels&#8230; eh? It goes through the motions, and it certainly poses a plausible scenario of how 2472 can be so dangerous. However, what makes 2472 work is the fact that it's something so mundane and unanomalous that causes everything to freak out, and people to question their perception. Shouldn't it be, then, that the opposite can happen? Something so dangerous and threatening that no one cares about and no one can even detect? That's what I took from 2472.</p>
<p>This takes an easy and direct route to answer &quot;What makes 2472 dangerous?&quot;, but doesn't feel like it follows up much on that. I'm thinking on this.</p>

							</div>

								
					
